# content.zd — the posts `site.zd` publishes.
#
# A module is a unit of naming rather than of deployment (§14D.2), so the
# `static` list that a route parameter ranges over may live in one file
# and the `route` that enumerates it in another.
#
# Reading these from `content/*.md` needs the foreign function interface
# (§14E), which does not exist yet. Everything here is therefore written
# out — which is honest about what the compiler can evaluate at build
# time today, and changes nothing about the routing: the route reads a
# `static` list either way.

# Every post, in publication order. `static`, so the build host holds
# the whole list and the route can enumerate it.
state slugs is static List of Text starting ["routing", "folding"]

# Read by the home page and by nothing else, so it is in the home page's
# bundle and in no other. §16.3.1's dead-code claim, per document.
function tagline with count
    give "Five URLs, one program, one document each."

function titleOf with slug
    if slug is "routing"
        give "Routing without a page"
    otherwise
        give "Folding an address"

function bodyOf with slug
    if slug is "routing"
        give "A route is a choice plus a bijection onto URLs."
    otherwise
        give "An immutable signal has one value per document."
